"""TCPP01-M12: USB Type-C port protection for sink applications with reference circuit.

Single-chip Type-C port protection from STMicroelectronics in a QFN-12L
3x3 mm package:

- 22 V tolerant ESD (IEC 61000-4-2 Level 4, ±8 kV contact / ±15 kV air) on
  CC1, CC2 and VBUS connector lines.
- 22 V short-to-VBUS OVP on CC lines (internal back-to-back FETs from
  CCx_c -> CCx).
- Externally programmable VBUS OVP via an N-MOSFET pass switch driven by
  GATE / monitored via VBUS_CTRL.
- "Dead-battery" management on DB/ for USB-PD compliant attach.
- Open-drain FLT/ for OVP/OTP/UVLO fault reporting.

Reference circuitry included (always-on):

- `C_VCC` (100 nF, 0402): VCC decoupling on pin 12.
- `C_ESD` (100 nF, 0402, 50 V X7R): IN_GD ESD shunt. Datasheet §6.6.1 makes
  this mandatory for the IC's advertised ±8 kV contact / IEC 61000-4-2 L4
  rating. Size ≤ 0603 is called out for low ESL; 0402 is preferred.
- `R_OVP_TOP` / `R_OVP_BOT`: VBUS_CTRL divider that programs the external
  N-MOSFET OVP trip via the internal reference V_ovp_th = 1.27 V typ
  (§3 Table 6). R_BOT fixed at 18 kΩ; R_TOP computed from
  `vbus_ovp_threshold`. Default 22 V covers full PD range (VBUS_abs_max);
  set to ~6 V for 5 V-only sinks (§6.7).
- `R_FLT` (100 kΩ): pull-up on the open-drain FLT/ flag to VCC.

Not included (use-case specific, left to the integrator):

- External N-MOSFET on VBUS (GATE/SOURCE) — driven to 5–6 V Vgs; choose per
  load current (up to 5 A), Vgs rating, and R_DS(on) budget (§6.6.7).
- Dead-battery network on DB/ — handled by the MCU GPIO or tied low; the
  IC provides an internal 5 kΩ pull-down.
- CC line EMI capacitors — required only for USB-PD (§6.6.4); value must be
  budgeted against the downstream MCU's CC pin capacitance.
- VBUS bulk cap (2.2 µF min) and VBUS TVS (e.g. ESDA25P35-1U1M) — system-
  level, not protection-IC-level.

Reference: ST DS12900 Rev 7 (https://www.st.com/resource/en/datasheet/tcpp01-m12.pdf).
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Voltage", "Resistance")
load("@stdlib/utils.zen", "e96")

Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")
Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")

# Power
VCC = io(Power(voltage="3.0V to 3.6V"), help="3.3 V supply. Tie LOW to fully power down the IC (zero Iq).")
GND = io(Ground(), help="Device ground and exposed pad.")

# Connector-side (USB-C receptacle) pins
CC1C = io(Net, help="Connector-side CC1. Wire directly to USB-C CC1.")
CC2C = io(Net, help="Connector-side CC2. Wire directly to USB-C CC2.")
IN_GD = io(Power(voltage="0V to 22V"), help="Connector-side VBUS. Tie to USB-C VBUS at the connector.")

# System-side CC pins (after internal back-to-back OVP FETs)
CC1 = io(Net, help="System-side CC1. Connect to MCU/UCPD CC1.")
CC2 = io(Net, help="System-side CC2. Connect to MCU/UCPD CC2.")

# External VBUS pass-MOSFET driver
SOURCE = io(Power(voltage="0V to 22V"), help="External NMOS source. System-side VBUS rail after the protection FET.")
GATE = io(Net, help="External NMOS gate drive.")
VBUS_CTRL = io(Net, help="VBUS OVP sense. MCU can force FET off by driving '1'.")

# Control / status
DB = io(Net, help="Dead-battery network. Pull-down resistor enables Rd advertisement at unpowered attach.")
FLT = io(Net, help="Open-drain fault flag. Asserted low on OVP/OTP/UVLO.")

vbus_ovp_threshold = config(Voltage, default="22V", help="VBUS OVP trip. 22V = full PD; 6V = 5V-only.")
add_flt_pullup = config(bool, default=True, help="Populate the FLT/ pull-up to VCC.")


def vbus_divider(v_trip):
    """§3 Table 6: V_ovp_th = 1.27 V typ. R_BOT fixed at 18 kΩ (≈70 µA at 22 V)."""
    V_TH = Voltage("1.27V")
    r_bot = Resistance("18kohm")
    r_top = r_bot * (v_trip / V_TH - 1)
    return e96(r_top), r_bot


_R_OVP_TOP, _R_OVP_BOT = vbus_divider(vbus_ovp_threshold)

Component(
    name="U",
    symbol=Symbol(library="TCPP01-M12.kicad_sym", name="TCPP01-M12"),
    footprint=File("QFN-12-1EP_3x3mm_P0.5mm_EP1.45x1.45mm.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="TCPP01-M12", manufacturer="STMicroelectronics"),
    pins={
        "VCC": VCC,
        "GND": GND,
        "EP": GND,
        "CC1_{c}": CC1C,
        "CC2_{c}": CC2C,
        "IN_{GD}": IN_GD,
        "CC1": CC1,
        "CC2": CC2,
        "SOURCE": SOURCE,
        "GATE": GATE,
        "VBUS_{CTRL}": VBUS_CTRL,
        "DB/": DB,
        "FLT/": FLT,
    },
)

# VCC decoupling (pin 12).
Capacitor(name="C_VCC", value="100nF", package="0402", P1=VCC, P2=GND)

# IN_GD ESD shunt — datasheet §6.6.1. Mandatory for the IC's ±8 kV contact
# IEC 61000-4-2 L4 rating. 50 V X7R, ≤0603 for low ESL (0402 preferred).
Capacitor(name="C_ESD", value="100nF", package="0402", voltage="50V", P1=IN_GD, P2=GND)

# VBUS_CTRL OVP divider. R_TOP computed so V(VBUS_CTRL) = 1.27 V at the
# chosen VBUS trip point. MCU GPIO on VBUS_CTRL can still override (HighZ
# for normal, drive '1' to force the external NMOS off) — §6.6.7.
Resistor(name="R_OVP_TOP", value=_R_OVP_TOP, package="0402", P1=IN_GD, P2=VBUS_CTRL)
Resistor(name="R_OVP_BOT", value=_R_OVP_BOT, package="0402", P1=VBUS_CTRL, P2=GND)

# FLT/ is open-drain (§1 Table 1); pull up to VCC for a readable logic level.
Resistor(name="R_FLT", value="100kohm", package="0402", dnp=not add_flt_pullup, P1=FLT, P2=VCC)

Layout(name="TCPP01-M12", path="layout/TCPP01-M12")

